& [Delineation]
  + canonical request is the deterministic full-prefix value required by existing IterationRecord replay
  + actual request is the experimental packet projected for possible model-facing transport
  + structural correspondence permits both to govern the same response admission inputs but does not make their model semantics equal
  + provider-free projection constructs evidence and does not claim any packet was sent or received
  + canonical wrapper authority remains unchanged and contains no compact transport claim

& [SelectedForms]
  + AttentionTransportRecord places actual request frame and canonical iteration side by side
  + first transport has full-prefix kind and no frame while later transports have compact-reentry kind and exact recomputed frames
  + TerminalReflectionTransport preserves both actual compact and canonical full reflection requests plus the same sanitized final response
  + ScriptedCompactTransportProjection wraps the unmodified complete run with ordered transport evidence and denial flags
  + validation begins with complete-wrapper validation then reconstructs every prefix request frame response and terminal mapping

& [FacultyReview]
  + Honesty prevents actual transport from being rewritten as canonical history or synthetic projection from being called provider execution
  + Security validates the canonical complete wrapper before deriving or admitting transport correspondence
  + Planner requires exactly one record per iteration with first-versus-later kind rules
  + Weaver maps each compact frame to its retained canonical prefix and terminal response
  + Scribe preserves both request identities and shared sanitized response evidence
  + Refiner avoids duplicating exact registry bodies into transport records
  + Observer admits the wrapper only when canonical replay and every actual transport reconstruction agree

& [Decision]
  + activate isolated dual_transcript projection generator validator normalizer and focused tests
  + retain live execution provider transport and default replacement under separate locks

& [Rollback]
  + additive module exports and tests remove without changing predecessor forms or behavior
